{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d user interface 3 d user interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md","fileName":"3D User Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D User Interface","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","User Interface","3D Interaction","Virtual Environment","Input Device","Output Device","Interaction Technique","3D Manipulation","3D Travel","Wayfinding","System Control","Virtual Reality","Augmented Reality","Telerobotics","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d user interface 3 d user interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md","fileName":"3D User Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D User Interface","heading":"3D User Interface","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A 3D user interface is a [[User Interface]] that involves [[3D Interaction]]. It may combine spatial input, visual, auditory, or haptic output, and software mappings that let a person act in a real or [[Virtual Environment|virtual]] three-dimensional context.\n\nIts main components are [[Input Device]]s, [[Output Device]]s, and [[Interaction Technique]]s. Common task families include [[3D Manipulation]], [[3D Travel]], [[Wayfinding]], and [[System Control]]. Good design requires these parts to work together; individually usable techniques do not automatically form a coherent interface.\n\n3D interfaces appear in [[Virtual Reality]], [[Augmented Reality]], design, training, games, data analysis, medicine, collaboration, and [[Telerobotics]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","User Interface","3D Interaction","Virtual Environment","Input Device","Output Device","Interaction Technique","3D Manipulation","3D Travel","Wayfinding","System Control","Virtual Reality","Augmented Reality","Telerobotics","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d user interface 3 d user interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D User Interface.md","fileName":"3D User Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D User Interface","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","User Interface","3D Interaction","Virtual Environment","Input Device","Output Device","Interaction Technique","3D Manipulation","3D Travel","Wayfinding","System Control","Virtual Reality","Augmented Reality","Telerobotics","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}